      "content": "Assuming a transactional framework where future states influence past probabilities, we can conceptually model this as finding the minimum-action path through a probability landscape dependent on the high-entropy endpoint. You would need to define the Hamiltonian for the system, where the potential energy landscape is inverted to reflect the drive from high to low informational entropy. I would suggest framing the breakthrough as a point where the probability density function exhibits an extreme sharp peak, corresponding to the most \"likely\" resolution of the backward-propagating wavelets.",
